      "id": "thread-context-abi",
      "title": "Resolve FreeBSD thread context and join-result assertions",
      "disposition": "architecture-specific",
      "reason": "Exact source review identifies three F-Stack/FreeBSD-specific assertions: opaque pcurthread pointer inheritance, discarding a non-NULL start result through a join result slot absent from LKL, and a test-local FreeBSD PCPU_GET null-context panic mirror that never creates a thread. Preserve original Linux task/TLS and the pinned LKL void-start/handle-only-join ABI. These are explicitly excluded, not Ker passes; source IDs and executable alternative boundaries are documented.",
      "evidence": [
        "src/posix/host-thread.c",
        "tests/upstream/fstack/tests/unit/test_ff_thread.c",
        "docs/fstack-thread-contracts.md"
      ],
      "acceptance": [
        "Retain each exact source assertion and pinned provenance; do not count Linux thread/TLS tests as these FreeBSD ABI passes.",
        "Keep the real native-fstack-thread-runtime argument/allocation-failure adaptations and runtime extensions separately qualified.",
        "Reopen adaptation only if an actual Ker consumer requires the source-specific ABI; do not synthesize FreeBSD task/PCPU pointers or alter upstream LKL callback signatures merely for a test."
      ],
      "cases": [
        "tests/unit/test_ff_thread.c::test_ff_pthread_create_basic",
        "tests/unit/test_ff_thread.c::test_ff_pthread_join_retval",
