      "id": "freebsd-internals",
      "title": "Record nonportable callout, kqueue, mbuf and page-array build assertions",
      "disposition": "architecture-specific",
      "reason": "These assertions depend on FreeBSD sbintime/hardclock/tick conversion, timer activation macros, internal kqueue filter IDs or mbuf M_PKTHDR/m_pkthdr.len fields. Original Linux has different timer/readiness/skb representations; a VMA payload or fabricated FreeBSD header mirror does not qualify them. The FF_USE_PAGE_ARRAY reload restriction depends on process-private FreeBSD bsd_m_table references, with a conditional reject/on and accept/off source pair; it is not a generic Linux allocator contract.",
      "evidence": [
        "tests/upstream/fstack/tests/unit/test_ff_callout.c",
        "tests/upstream/fstack/tests/unit/test_ff_epoll.c",
        "src/posix/posix-poll.c",
